        devotion: 'Daniel was told his routine of prayer would get him thrown to the lions. He kept doing it anyway. When everything around him was threatening his life, he fell back on his habits. That is the power of routine — it holds you when willpower fails. Recovery requires building a new daily structure that replaces the hours, rituals, and patterns that used to revolve around the substance.',
        reflection_q: 'What does your ideal recovery day look like from waking to sleeping? What routines are you building that will hold you when willpower runs out?',
