        devotion: 'Twenty-eight days. You made it. You were honest when it hurt. You rebuilt your identity when shame tried to name you. You created new patterns when old ones pulled at you. You reached out when isolation called. And today, Jesus speaks over you the same words He spoke 2,000 years ago: "You are free indeed." Not free-ish. Not mostly free. Not free until the next craving. FREE INDEED. The chains are broken. The cell door is open. And the road ahead is wide, bright, and full of purpose. This is not the end of your recovery — it is the foundation. Keep going. Keep showing up. Keep surrendering. And when the hard days come — and they will — remember: you have already proven that freedom is possible.',
